<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:23:12 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>观看欧洲欧几里得太空望远镜拍摄到的令人惊叹的宇宙图像，该望远镜正在绘制最大的 3D 宇宙地图</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-stunning-images-of-the-universe-captured-by-europes-euclid-space-telescope-which-is-buildling-the-biggest-3d-map-of-the-cosmos-180989884/</link><description>这 170 万 GB 的数据包括超过 9 亿个星系、超过 6000 万个潜在类星体以及大约 15,000 个难以捉摸的宇宙现象的候选者，该现象可以帮助科学家了解暗物质和暗能量</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:32:47 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-stunning-images-of-the-universe-captured-by-europes-euclid-space-telescope-which-is-buildling-the-biggest-3d-map-of-the-cosmos-180989884/</guid></item><item><title>吉娃娃似乎带有一点土狼的 DNA，但这可能不是它们拥有无所畏惧的性格的原因</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/chihuahuas-seem-to-carry-a-tiny-bit-of-coyote-dna-but-thats-probably-not-why-they-have-fearless-personalities-180989886/</link><description>新研究表明，郊狼 DNA 约占吉娃娃基因组的 0.1%，这可能是很久以前郊狼与家养狗祖先杂交的结果</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/chihuahuas-seem-to-carry-a-tiny-bit-of-coyote-dna-but-thats-probably-not-why-they-have-fearless-personalities-180989886/</guid></item><item><title>这个人来自丹麦的一个小岛，经历了 6000 年前从狩猎采集到农耕的转变</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/from-a-small-island-in-denmark-this-man-lived-through-the-transition-from-hunter-gathering-to-farming-6000-years-ago-180989889/</link><description>对罗达尔斯人的一项新分析表明，他在一生中目睹了新石器时代革命，在成长过程中主要吃海鲜，然后在成年后转向更多的陆地食物（可能是养殖食物）</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:15:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/from-a-small-island-in-denmark-this-man-lived-through-the-transition-from-hunter-gathering-to-farming-6000-years-ago-180989889/</guid></item><item><title>这种微小、不起眼的真菌是一种“黑暗魔法蘑菇”——第一个被发现含有迷幻化合物和致命毒素的蘑菇</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-tiny-unassuming-fungus-is-a-dark-magic-mushroom-the-first-found-to-contain-both-psychedelic-compounds-and-deadly-toxins-180989885/</link><description>研究人员从佛罗里达州中部湿地长满青苔的棕榈树干中采集了这种蘑菇。众所周知，它的亲戚会产生鹅膏毒素，但这种真菌在处理时却令人惊讶地变成蓝色，这是该生物体产生裸盖菇素的明显迹象</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:06:13 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-tiny-unassuming-fungus-is-a-dark-magic-mushroom-the-first-found-to-contain-both-psychedelic-compounds-and-deadly-toxins-180989885/</guid></item><item><title>古埃及的圣猫是如何生活的？ 100多具被拆开的木乃伊揭示了其恶劣的生活条件、感染和生前的暴力行为</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/how-did-ancient-egypts-sacred-cats-live-more-than-100-unwrapped-mummies-reveal-poor-living-conditions-infections-and-violence-before-death-180989888/</link><description>对 131 件博物馆标本进行的骨学和化学测试显示，后来被制成木乃伊的家猫和野生捕获的丛林猫患病率和身体创伤率很高</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:58:18 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/how-did-ancient-egypts-sacred-cats-live-more-than-100-unwrapped-mummies-reveal-poor-living-conditions-infections-and-violence-before-death-180989888/</guid></item><item><title>近 600 年来，这幅神秘的扬·凡·艾克 (Jan van Eyck) 画作一直让观众着迷。这真的是一幅乔装的自画像吗？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/for-almost-600-years-this-enigmatic-jan-van-eyck-painting-has-entraced-viewers-could-it-actually-be-a-self-portrait-in-disguise-180989883/</link><description>关于“阿尔诺菲尼肖像”的新理论诞生之​​际，伦敦国家美术馆首次汇集了该艺术家所有 10 幅已知肖像画</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:32:16 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/for-almost-600-years-this-enigmatic-jan-van-eyck-painting-has-entraced-viewers-could-it-actually-be-a-self-portrait-in-disguise-180989883/</guid></item><item><title>SpaceX 首次捕捉到其星际飞船的上级，使该公司距离可重复使用火箭又近了一步</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/spacex-catches-the-upper-stage-of-its-starship-for-the-first-time-making-the-company-one-step-closer-to-a-reusable-rocket-180989877/</link><description>绕地球 14 圈后，星舰的上部下降到地球表面，并被一对巨大的筷子状机械臂抓住。然而，该公司未能抢占其先前展示过的下层舞台</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/spacex-catches-the-upper-stage-of-its-starship-for-the-first-time-making-the-company-one-step-closer-to-a-reusable-rocket-180989877/</guid></item><item><title>美国已经失去了维持了 26 年的麻疹消除地位。案件现已激增至数十年来的最高水平</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-us-has-lost-its-measles-elimination-status-which-its-held-for-26-years-cases-have-now-surged-to-the-highest-levels-in-decades-180989878/</link><description>今年迄今为止，疾病控制与预防中心已确认超过 5,400 例麻疹病例（这是自 1991 年以来的最高年度病例总数），并爆发了 43 起麻疹疫情。疫苗接种率下降可能是罪魁祸首</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-us-has-lost-its-measles-elimination-status-which-its-held-for-26-years-cases-have-now-surged-to-the-highest-levels-in-decades-180989878/</guid></item><item><title>125,000 年前，古代人类可能在阿拉伯半岛用有毒的矛尖猎杀河马</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/ancient-humans-may-have-hunted-hippos-with-poisoned-spear-tips-on-the-arabian-peninsula-125000-years-ago-180989880/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，人们在现在沙特阿拉伯南部的一个茂密的大型淡水湖附近狩猎和加工野味，这挑战了人类刚刚经过该地区的假设</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:10:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/ancient-humans-may-have-hunted-hippos-with-poisoned-spear-tips-on-the-arabian-peninsula-125000-years-ago-180989880/</guid></item><item><title>布鲁姆斯伯里集团的凡妮莎·贝尔和邓肯·格兰特几十年来一直将他们的艺术和生活纠缠在一起。贝尔临终前的最后一幅草图在 60 年后重新浮出水面</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-bloomsbury-groups-vanessa-bell-and-duncan-grant-tangled-their-art-and-lives-together-for-decades-a-final-sketch-of-bell-on-her-deathbed-just-resurfaced-after-60-years-180989874/</link><description>这两位艺术家的关系非常复杂，还有一个女儿，但他们从未停止互相绘画。这一新发现表明了一种贯穿健康和疾病的艺术纽带</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:28:51 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-bloomsbury-groups-vanessa-bell-and-duncan-grant-tangled-their-art-and-lives-together-for-decades-a-final-sketch-of-bell-on-her-deathbed-just-resurfaced-after-60-years-180989874/</guid></item><item><title>这些可爱的幼龟来自美国西海岸第一个已知的天然海龟巢。现在，他们又回到了野外</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-adorable-hatchlings-are-from-the-us-west-coasts-first-known-natural-sea-turtle-nests-now-theyve-returned-to-the-wild-180989876/</link><description>九月份发现了两个鸟巢，当局将这些蛋转移到水族馆，以保护它们免受即将到来的热带风暴的影响。周末，数十只幼龟出现，现已在被发现的同一海滩被释放</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:08:45 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-adorable-hatchlings-are-from-the-us-west-coasts-first-known-natural-sea-turtle-nests-now-theyve-returned-to-the-wild-180989876/</guid></item><item><title>法国法院宣布以 160 万美元出售这幅卡米尔·毕沙罗 (Camille Pissarro) 画作，据称该画作在二战期间被掠夺</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-french-court-annuls-the-sale-of-this-camille-pissarro-painting-allegedly-looted-during-world-war-ii-180989875/</link><description>犹太银行家所罗门·弗拉维安 (Salomon Flavian) 的七名后裔对 2024 年在他们不知情的情况下进行的拍卖提出质疑，促使法院要求归还这幅画并透露匿名买家的身份</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:29:33 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-french-court-annuls-the-sale-of-this-camille-pissarro-painting-allegedly-looted-during-world-war-ii-180989875/</guid></item><item><title>地球地质记录中缺失了超过十亿年的岩层。科学家说他们可能终于知道原因了</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/more-than-a-billion-years-worth-of-rock-layers-are-missing-from-earths-geologic-record-scientists-say-they-may-finally-know-why-180989870/</link><description>计算机模拟表明，地球粘性地幔层的运动抬升了地球表面的某些块，使冰盖刮掉了岩石</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:48:38 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/more-than-a-billion-years-worth-of-rock-layers-are-missing-from-earths-geologic-record-scientists-say-they-may-finally-know-why-180989870/</guid></item><item><title>欧洲赫拉飞船已开始对 NASA 于 2022 年有意撞击的小行星系统进行近距离调查</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/europes-hera-spacecraft-has-begun-its-close-up-investigation-of-the-asteroid-system-nasa-intentionally-hit-in-2022-180989871/</link><description>欧洲航天局的任务将提供有关计划中碰撞后果的宝贵数据，这些数据可以为行星防御措施提供信息并揭示有关小行星的见解</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/europes-hera-spacecraft-has-begun-its-close-up-investigation-of-the-asteroid-system-nasa-intentionally-hit-in-2022-180989871/</guid></item><item><title>这些伦敦公寓看起来完全是石器时代的风格。它们会成为可持续建筑的未来吗？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-london-apartments-look-straight-from-the-stone-age-could-they-be-the-future-of-sustianable-architecture-180989873/</link><description>一个新的住宅区采用由 1,000 吨原石制成的承重外骨骼，为碳密集型钢和混凝土结构提供了替代方案。它的设计师认为过去的纪念性石头建筑正在重新流行</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:15:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-london-apartments-look-straight-from-the-stone-age-could-they-be-the-future-of-sustianable-architecture-180989873/</guid></item><item><title>这条青铜腿从苏格兰沼泽中出现两个世纪后，考古学家认为它可能属于马背上罗马皇帝的高耸雕像</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-centuries-after-this-bronze-leg-emerged-from-a-scottish-bog-archaeologists-believe-it-may-have-once-belonged-to-a-towering-statue-of-a-roman-emperor-on-horseback-180989872/</link><description>长期以来，人们一直认为这条具有传奇色彩的腿是被苏格兰部落从英格兰北部掠夺来的，但在被撤退的军队小心地拆除和掩埋之前，这条具有传奇色彩的腿实际上可能在罗马时期的苏格兰展示过。</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:34:46 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-centuries-after-this-bronze-leg-emerged-from-a-scottish-bog-archaeologists-believe-it-may-have-once-belonged-to-a-towering-statue-of-a-roman-emperor-on-horseback-180989872/</guid></item><item><title>永久冻土融化可能会造成一种新型山体滑坡，随着世界变暖，这种滑坡可能会变得更加常见</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/thawing-permafrost-may-have-created-a-new-type-of-landslide-which-could-become-more-common-as-the-world-warms-180989863/</link><description>科学家将这一事件称为永久冻土分离滑移。这些山体滑坡并非自上而下解冻，而是源自薄弱的基础</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:33:14 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/thawing-permafrost-may-have-created-a-new-type-of-landslide-which-could-become-more-common-as-the-world-warms-180989863/</guid></item><item><title>英国考古学家在一条沟渠中发现了 8000 块罗马时代的青蛙骨头。他们刚刚解开了两栖动物如何到达那里的谜团</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-in-england-discovered-8000-roman-era-frog-bones-in-a-single-ditch-they-just-solved-the-mystery-how-the-amphibians-ended-up-there-180989868/</link><description>新研究表明，大约 1700 年前，短耳猫头鹰等中型猛禽在一次“短暂而密集的捕食事件”中以青蛙为食</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:25:49 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-in-england-discovered-8000-roman-era-frog-bones-in-a-single-ditch-they-just-solved-the-mystery-how-the-amphibians-ended-up-there-180989868/</guid></item><item><title>美国宇航局的四名宇航员在“火星”上度过了一年多的时间。这是他们在模拟火星栖息地 378 天所做的事情</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-four-person-nasa-crew-spent-over-a-year-on-mars-heres-what-they-did-for-378-days-in-a-simulated-martian-habitat-180989862/</link><description>经过严格的筛选过程和长期的准备工作，船员们得以在休斯敦 3D 打印的红色星球环境复制品中同居。在那里，他们练习火星行走，中断了与地球上人们的通讯和粮食种植</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-four-person-nasa-crew-spent-over-a-year-on-mars-heres-what-they-did-for-378-days-in-a-simulated-martian-habitat-180989862/</guid></item><item><title>德国文艺复兴大师阿尔布雷希特·阿尔特多费尔 (Albrecht Altdorfer) 开创了风景画。一部学者此前不为人知的作品在私人收藏 70 年后刚刚问世</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/german-renaissance-master-albrecht-altdorfer-pioneered-landscape-painting-a-work-previously-unknown-to-scholars-just-emerged-after-70-years-in-a-private-collection-180989861/</link><description>这幅新发现的画作于 1520 年左右绘制，是该艺术家仅有的三幅纯油画风景画之一。它描绘了郁郁葱葱的森林场景，城堡废墟和暴风雨天空中出现的彩虹</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:02:16 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/german-renaissance-master-albrecht-altdorfer-pioneered-landscape-painting-a-work-previously-unknown-to-scholars-just-emerged-after-70-years-in-a-private-collection-180989861/</guid></item></channel></rss>